# Flutter Modular Styling Architecture

## Overview

The styling system has been refactored from a monolithic 792-line file into a clean, modular architecture located in [lib/styles/](mdc:lib/styles).

## File Structure

### Core Files
- **[lib/styles/styles.dart](mdc:lib/styles/styles.dart)** - Barrel export for all style modules
- **[lib/styles/themes.dart](mdc:lib/styles/themes.dart)** - Global app themes (light/dark)
- **[lib/styles/global_styles.dart](mdc:lib/styles/global_styles.dart)** - Shared colors, shadows, text styles

### Component-Specific Files
- **[lib/styles/onboarding_styles.dart](mdc:lib/styles/onboarding_styles.dart)** - Splash screen and onboarding flows
- **[lib/styles/game_card_styles.dart](mdc:lib/styles/game_card_styles.dart)** - Game cards (portrait/landscape)
- **[lib/styles/layout_styles.dart](mdc:lib/styles/layout_styles.dart)** - Layout, sections, navigation
- **[lib/styles/input_styles.dart](mdc:lib/styles/input_styles.dart)** - Search bars, buttons, dropdowns

### Legacy Compatibility
- **[lib/styles/main_screen_styles.dart](mdc:lib/styles/main_screen_styles.dart)** - Backward compatibility layer

## Usage Patterns

### Preferred Import (New Code)
```dart
// Import specific modules for better performance
import '../styles/game_card_styles.dart';
import '../styles/global_styles.dart';

Container(
  decoration: GameCardStyles.gameCardDecoration,
  child: Text('Game Title', style: TextStyle(color: AppColors.primaryText)),
);
```

### Legacy Import (Existing Code)
```dart
// Still works for backward compatibility
import '../styles/styles.dart';
Container(decoration: MainScreenStyles.gameCardDecoration);
```

## Style Classes

### AppColors (Global Palette)
- `AppColors.primaryAccent` - Main brand color
- `AppColors.primaryText` - Primary text color
- `AppColors.background` - Main background
- `AppColors.collapsibleSection` - Section backgrounds

### Component Style Classes
- `GameCardStyles` - All game card related styling
- `LayoutStyles` - Layout and structural styling
- `InputStyles` - Interactive component styling
- `CollapsibleSectionStyles` - Section component styling
- `EmptyStateStyles` - Empty state styling

## Migration Guidelines

### For New Components
1. Use modular style classes directly (`GameCardStyles.xxx`)
2. Import only the style modules you need
3. Use `AppColors` for color values
4. Use `AppShadows` for shadow definitions

### For Existing Components
1. Continue using `MainScreenStyles` (backward compatible)
2. Gradually migrate during updates
3. Test compatibility when making changes

### Adding New Styles
1. Identify the appropriate style module
2. Add styles to the relevant class
3. Use semantic naming conventions
4. Update [lib/styles/main_screen_styles.dart](mdc:lib/styles/main_screen_styles.dart) if needed for compatibility

## Best Practices

### Naming Conventions
- **Semantic Names**: `primaryAccent` vs `orangeColor`
- **Component Prefixes**: `gameCard`, `collapsibleSection`
- **Size Descriptors**: `small`, `compact`, `landscape`
- **State Indicators**: `selected`, `expanded`, `disabled`

### Organization Principles
- **Single Responsibility**: Each file handles one concern
- **Logical Grouping**: Related styles in same class
- **Import Efficiency**: Easy to import what you need
- **Consistent Structure**: Same pattern across all files

### Performance Tips
- Import specific modules instead of the barrel export when possible
- Use tree-shaking friendly imports
- Prefer `AppColors` and `AppShadows` for reusable values

## Architecture Benefits

✅ **Modular Organization** - Easy to find and modify specific styles
✅ **Better Performance** - Import only what you need
✅ **Team Collaboration** - Multiple developers can work on different style files
✅ **Maintainability** - Changes isolated to specific files
✅ **Backward Compatibility** - Existing code continues to work
